  "reason": "Evidence: The top-5 configs all use scvi_n200 + multiprofile, with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion yielding the best accuracy (config_049: 0.724989). Notably, config_013 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) achieved the highest F1 of any experiment (0.694524) despite slightly lower accuracy (0.713087), suggesting resnet50 captures complementary spatial features. Question: Does the resnet50 + transformer combination with concat fusion (rather than weighted) unlock a different accuracy/F1 tradeoff that could approach or exceed 0.725? This is the only untested multiprofile scvi_n200 configuration combining transformer aggregation with resnet50 and concat fusion. Rationale: As the final experiment, this is the most logical exploitation of the proven scvi_n200 + transformer family while testing the one unexplored image-encoder/fusion pairing that showed the strongest F1 signal. Expected cost is moderate (~5-6 GPU hours), comparable to config_013 (6.22) and config_009 (4.65), keeping total budget reasonable."
